1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,682
The Ratchet Lady: she once loved helping people.

2
00:00:02,682 --> 00:00:05,164
Now there's still a smile, but it's a hateful one.

3
00:00:05,384 --> 00:00:06,685
Here's how she plays.

4
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:11,901
Put the six red Maniac meeples in a pile next to the Victims, and place two Maniacs

5
00:00:11,901 --> 00:00:16,142
in the Ratchet Lady's starting space. Her two Calm Action cards go in the Action

6
00:00:16,142 --> 00:00:16,567
Tableau.

7
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:21,553
She starts with only six health, but she has no upper limit, and lots of her cards

8
00:00:21,553 --> 00:00:24,745
heal her. Her Bloodlust track also heals her at certain levels.

9
00:00:24,745 --> 00:00:26,872
She can grow far beyond where she started.

10
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:31,740
Maniacs are Victims driven mad. They're Minions, with one health, and attack and

11
00:00:31,740 --> 00:00:34,719
movement of one. They won't follow you, and can't be saved.

12
00:00:34,939 --> 00:00:37,721
When a Victim becomes a Maniac, swap in a red meeple.

13
00:00:37,721 --> 00:00:42,078
Bloodlust doesn't rise, as no one died. When you kill a Maniac, it goes back in the

14
00:00:42,078 --> 00:00:43,600
pool, and again no Bloodlust.

15
00:00:43,820 --> 00:00:46,493
Only normal Victims turn, never Special Victims.

16
00:00:46,493 --> 00:00:50,113
And there's a limit of six on the board: ignore any extra spawns.

17
00:00:50,933 --> 00:00:55,050
Maniacs grab at you. If there are Maniacs in your space and you leave, you lose one

18
00:00:55,050 --> 00:00:57,035
health for each Maniac beyond the first.

19
00:00:57,255 --> 00:01:01,073
So one Maniac is no problem, but with three, leaving costs you two health.

20
00:01:01,900 --> 00:01:06,353
Calm turns Maniacs back into Victims. It costs two Time, and works on Maniacs in

21
00:01:06,353 --> 00:01:08,023
your space or an adjacent one.

22
00:01:08,243 --> 00:01:12,700
Two successes calm up to two Maniacs. One success calms one, and ends your turn.

23
00:01:12,700 --> 00:01:17,046
With no successes, one still calms, but Bloodlust rises and your turn ends, or

24
00:01:17,046 --> 00:01:19,720
instead you can take a Horror and lose two Time.

25
00:01:19,940 --> 00:01:23,673
Calmed Victims follow you, can be saved, and can be killed by Enemies again.

26
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:28,884
Her Dark Powers. Bloodfear: in each Killer phase, the first time Horror or Bloodlust

27
00:01:28,884 --> 00:01:33,215
goes up, she heals one. Dark Injection: the first time she heals each Killer phase,

28
00:01:33,215 --> 00:01:34,207
she heals one more.

29
00:01:34,427 --> 00:01:38,032
Manic Burst: every new Maniac immediately takes its Minion action.

30
00:01:38,252 --> 00:01:40,433
And her Epic Dark Power, Shield of Madness:

31
00:01:40,433 --> 00:01:43,223
she can't lose health while any Maniac is on the board.

32
00:01:44,033 --> 00:01:48,115
Her Finales. Feed the Madness heals her every Killer phase and spawns a Maniac

33
00:01:48,115 --> 00:01:52,353
whenever there are none. It's Raining Maniacs spawns two more every Killer phase.

34
00:01:52,573 --> 00:01:56,902
Hold Her Down turns every remaining Victim into a Maniac and removes your Calm

35
00:01:56,902 --> 00:02:00,509
cards. And the Epic Finale spawns four Maniacs and heals her six.

36
00:02:01,333 --> 00:02:06,005
A few tips. Calmed Maniacs become Victims you can save, so Calm and rescue together.

37
00:02:06,225 --> 00:02:09,852
Killing a Maniac doesn't raise Bloodlust, so it's often the quicker option.

38
00:02:10,072 --> 00:02:13,382
And strike her early with big attacks, before her healing snowballs.

39
00:02:13,382 --> 00:02:13,869
Good luck.

